In swimlane mode, each column/lane cell is just a `<div>` and isn’t registered as a droppable target with a stable id. This prevents dropping into empty cells / appending to an empty lane, because `handleDragEnd` only understands destinations when `overId` is a card id or a column id. Add a droppable per cell (or reuse column droppables) and map that droppable id back to the destination column in `handleDragEnd`.
```suggestion
                          <SortableContext
                            id={`${col.id}::${lane}`}
                            items={laneCards.map(c => c.id)}
                            strategy={verticalListSortingStrategy}
                          >
```

`laneCardCount` is recomputed inside the `swimlanes.map` via `reduce(... filter ...)`, which is O(lanes × columns × cards) on every render. For larger boards this can become a noticeable bottleneck. Consider precomputing a lane->count map in a `useMemo` alongside `swimlanes` (and similarly precompute laneCards per column) to avoid repeated filtering.
```suggestion
          {/*
           * Precompute lane card counts and lane-specific cards per column.
           * This avoids O(lanes × columns × cards) repeated filtering on each render.
           */}
          {(() => {
            const { laneCardCountMap, laneCardsByLaneAndColumn } = React.useMemo(() => {
              const laneCardCountMap = new Map<string, number>()
              const laneCardsByLaneAndColumn: Record<string, Record<string, typeof boardColumns[number]["cards"]>> = {}

              for (const col of boardColumns) {
                const columnCardsByLane = new Map<string, typeof col.cards>()

                for (const card of col.cards) {
                  const laneKey =
                    card[swimlaneField!] != null
                      ? String(card[swimlaneField!])
                      : UNCATEGORIZED_LANE

                  // Update per-lane total count
                  laneCardCountMap.set(laneKey, (laneCardCountMap.get(laneKey) ?? 0) + 1)

                  // Group cards by lane and column
                  let laneCardsForColumn = columnCardsByLane.get(laneKey)
                  if (!laneCardsForColumn) {
                    laneCardsForColumn = []
                    columnCardsByLane.set(laneKey, laneCardsForColumn)
                  }
                  laneCardsForColumn.push(card)
                }

                // Persist column groups into the nested record structure
                for (const [laneKey, cardsForLane] of columnCardsByLane.entries()) {
                  if (!laneCardsByLaneAndColumn[laneKey]) {
                    laneCardsByLaneAndColumn[laneKey] = {}
                  }
                  laneCardsByLaneAndColumn[laneKey][col.id] = cardsForLane
                }
              }

              return { laneCardCountMap, laneCardsByLaneAndColumn }
            }, [boardColumns, swimlaneField])

            {/* Swimlane rows */}
            return swimlanes.map(lane => {
              const isCollapsed = collapsedLanes.has(lane)
              const laneCardCount = laneCardCountMap.get(lane) ?? 0

              return (
                <div key={lane} className="border rounded-lg bg-muted/10">
                  {/* Lane header */}
                  <button
                    className="w-full flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-left hover:bg-muted/30 transition-colors"
                    onClick={() => toggleLane(lane)}
                    aria-expanded={!isCollapsed}
                  >
                    <span className={cn("transition-transform text-xs", isCollapsed ? "" : "rotate-90")}>▶</span>
                    <span className="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">{lane}</span>
                    <span className="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">({laneCardCount})</span>
                  </button>

                  {/* Lane content */}
                  {!isCollapsed && (
                    <div className="flex gap-3 sm:gap-4 overflow-x-auto px-2 pb-3 pl-36 sm:pl-44">
                      {boardColumns.map(col => {
                        const laneCards =
                          laneCardsByLaneAndColumn[lane]?.[col.id] ?? []

                        return (
                          <div key={col.id} className="w-[85vw] sm:w-80 flex-shrink-0 min-h-[60px] rounded-md bg-card/20 p-2">
                            <SortableContext items={laneCards.map(c => c.id)} strategy={verticalListSortingStrategy}>
                              <div className="space-y-2" role="list" aria-label={`${col.title} - ${lane} cards`}>
                                {laneCards.map(card => (
                                  <SortableCard key={card.id} card={card} onCardClick={onCardClick} conditionalFormatting={conditionalFormatting} />
                                ))}
                              </div>
                            </SortableContext>
                          </div>
                        )
                      })}
                    </div>
                  )}
                </div>
              )
            })
          })()}
```

`activeUsers` falls back to `MOCK_PRESENCE_USERS` when `presenceUsers` isn’t passed, which will show fake online users in production (ConsoleLayout currently doesn’t pass `presenceUsers`). Gate the mock data behind a dev-only check and default to an empty list in production, or require real presence to be injected via props/context.
```suggestion
    const activeUsers =
      presenceUsers ??
      (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production' ? MOCK_PRESENCE_USERS : []);
```

`expiresAt` is computed by parsing `expiresIn` and calling `toISOString()`. If `expiresIn` is ever an unexpected value, `parseInt` can yield `NaN` and `toISOString()` will throw. Validate the parsed days value before constructing the date and omit `expiresAt` when invalid.
```suggestion
    let expiresAt: string | undefined;
    if (expiresIn) {
      const days = Number.parseInt(expiresIn, 10);
      if (Number.isFinite(days) && days > 0) {
        expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + days * 86400000).toISOString();
      }
    }
```

`MOCK_RECORD_VIEWERS` is defined as a non-empty constant and later rendered based on `MOCK_RECORD_VIEWERS.length > 0`, so the UI will always show fake viewers. Gate this to dev/mock mode or source it from real presence state and default to an empty array when unavailable.
```suggestion
// Optional demo presence users viewing the current record (empty by default)
const MOCK_RECORD_VIEWERS: PresenceUser[] = [];
```
